The 1982 tileset's source
=========================

Early-1980s fantasy pixel art at 32x32, in the DB16 palette.  An AI image
generator drew the pictures, sixteen to a sheet, to a brief written for this
game; the brief, every sheet it returned and the reasons each picture was
accepted or sent back are in archive/design_brief_tileset_1982/, which is
not in the repository.

    source.png      every accepted picture, cut to 32x32 and snapped to the
                    palette, on transparency.  This is the art.
    source.txt      which picture is where in source.png, and whether it is
                    fixed or recolourable
    recipe.txt      how each picture was cut from its sheet: the brief's
                    accepted.txt, copied here
    manifest.txt    which picture each terrain feature, object, trap, spell
                    effect and the player is drawn with
    monsters.txt    which picture each monster is drawn with

`build-1982.py` reads these and writes lib/tiles/1982/32x32.png and
graf-82.prf.  `build-1982.py --cut` rewrites source.png, source.txt and
monsters.txt from the brief's sheets, and needs the brief and ImageMagick.

Recolourable pictures
---------------------

A recolourable picture draws the part that changes colour in four greys
(#333333, #666666, #999999, #CCCCCC).  The build tints them with the thing's
own colour from lib/gamedata, keeping the shading, so one young dragon is
every young dragon and one potion bottle every potion, each the colour the
game says it is.

What the build adds
-------------------

  * The floor, drawn from the recipe: one plain iron slab per square with a
    bevelled joint.  `--cut` checks it against the brief's floor.png.
  * A one-pixel outline round every figure, object, trap and spell effect:
    ink, or stone round one nine-tenths darker than the floor, which ink does
    nothing for.
  * Rubble and the stairs laid on the floor, the buildings drawn on magenta
    laid on the town's grass, and each building's number or letter on its
    gable.
  * Each terrain feature in the game's four lights: as drawn when seen;
    warmed within the character's own light, which the game uses only when
    "Color: Illuminate torchlight in yellow" is on; dimmed and a little greyed
    when remembered, which the game calls `lit`; and dimmer still for the
    UNLIGHT case it calls `dark`.  A figure, object or trap has one tile; the
    front end lays it on the terrain and dims it when the square is
    remembered.
  * The heroine for a character whose $SEX is Female, which ui-prefs.c works
    out the way the Tk portraits do.

To change a picture, cut a new one into the brief's accepted.txt, copy that
here as recipe.txt, and run `build-1982.py --cut`.  To change which picture
something uses, edit manifest.txt or monsters.txt and run `build-1982.py`.
Check with `build-1982.py --check` and `audit-tiles.py`.
